\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


A symmetric polynomial is invariant under the specified permutations of its variables. Nonnegativity means its value is at least zero throughout the designated domain. A decidability question requires an effective encoding and quantification over the family of domains.
